PHASE 3 - VULNERABILITY ANALYSIS
Operation Iron Raven

1. OBSERVED TECHNOLOGIES

Web:
- Apache httpd 2.4.10 on Debian
- Raven Security website
- WordPress 4.8.7
- WordPress REST API
- WordPress XML-RPC
- WordPress login interface
- PHP endpoint: /contact.php

Network:
- SSH on TCP/22
- HTTP on TCP/80
- rpcbind on TCP/111
- RPC status service on TCP/43212

2. VERIFIED FACTS

- Target identified as 192.168.44.129.
- TCP/22 exposes OpenSSH 6.7p1.
- TCP/80 exposes Apache 2.4.10 on Debian.
- WordPress version 4.8.7 was observed.
- WordPress REST API is accessible.
- XML-RPC endpoint is present.
- WordPress login endpoint is accessible.
- RPC services are exposed through rpcbind/status.

3. UNVERIFIED ASSUMPTIONS

- Presence of an old software version does not by itself prove exploitability.
- An exposed REST API does not by itself prove unauthorized modification.
- An exposed XML-RPC endpoint does not by itself prove a usable attack condition.
- SSH exposure does not establish valid credentials.
- RPC exposure does not establish a privilege-escalation path.

4. POTENTIAL ATTACK SURFACES

A. WordPress installation
B. Web application/PHP endpoints
C. SSH service
D. RPC services

